To tell the full story: cancellation factor protects from magical results
of hand-to hand attacks (not only drain level - but also fire from 
fire ants, frost from yetis/giants etc). If you get hit by a creature with
such magic attack, the chances that you get the 'magic effect' (like felling 
hot with associated scroll burning) depend on the cancellation factor
approximately as you describe, i.e 100% for can=0, ~67% for can=1,
~35% for can=2, 2% for can=3.
Now, for level drain: if the cancellation did not protect you, there
is an additional roll, with 1/3 chance of actually getting drained. So to get
the table of level drain chances as a function of cancellation - multiply
everything by 1/3. This gives 1/150 for maximum cancellation (3) and about
11.5% for cancellation=2 (and 1/3 for cancellation=0).

And, to avoid misunderstandings: the cancellation does not come into play 
at all with ray attacks - only the AC counts there...
